---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
const updated = 'September 28, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of use" description={`The terms for using ${SITE.name}: a free resume builder you can use without an account. Your content is yours.`}>
  <article class="container-page max-w-3xl pt-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <div class="prose-content mt-8">
      <h2>Using the service</h2>
      <p>{SITE.name} is a free tool for writing resumes and CVs. You can use it without an account, for personal or professional job applications.</p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>What you write and import is yours. Because it's stored only in your browser, you're responsible for keeping backups (<em>File → Download backup</em>). We can't recover resumes that were deleted or lost when browser data was cleared.</p>

      <h2>Templates and examples</h2>
      <p>You may use any template for your own resumes and share or print the documents you make. The example resumes contain made-up people and details; don't present them as your own experience.</p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>You're responsible for making sure your resume is truthful. The writing ideas, resume check and job ad match are suggestions, not guarantees of how an employer or applicant tracking system will treat your application.</p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>The service is provided as it is, without warranties. We may change or discontinue features. We aren't liable for any loss arising from using it, to the extent the law allows.</p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Don't try to disrupt the site or use it to create misleading documents about other people.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
